<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wilhelm I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1797">1797</a>–<a href="/years/1888">1888</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wilhelm I was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> from 1861 and the first emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> from 1871 until his death in 1888. With his chancellor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-von-bismarck">Otto von Bismarck</a>, he presided over the wars against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> that united <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> under Prussian leadership. He was proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-emperor">German Emperor</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hall-of-mirrors">Hall of Mirrors</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a> in 1871.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wilhelm-i.jpg" alt="Wilhelm I" width="312" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wilhelm Kuntzemüller · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kaiser_Wilhelm_I_(3x4_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
